    "ldmia r0!, {{r4-r11}}", // pop callee-saved regs -> r0 addr moves 'up' to the hardware frame base
    "msr psp, r0", // move r0 into PSP (new stack lowest addr)
    "isb", // flush asm pipeline to ensure PSP is synchronised
    "bx r14", // trigger exception return -> HW pops hardware frame from PSP and resumes new task
The last comment (“HW pops … from PSP”) is only true if EXC_RETURN selects PSP; it is false for the MSP-thread case unless LR is fixed before bx.

2. Bug: bogus stack depth check (context_switch.rs)
The comment says the stack must be large enough for the head, but the condition compares stack_top’s numeric address to HEAD_SIZE_BYTES (e.g. 64). A valid RAM top like 0x20008000 always passes; you are not checking region size. The only failures are absurdly low “top” values.


