A real check needs stack base (or size) vs stack_top, not address vs 64.

3. Integration / ordering (not a line bug, but fragile)
PENDSV_NEXT_PSP and PENDSV_CURRENT_TASK are plain static mut assignments from Rust. The compiler may reorder ordinary writes relative to other code unless you use write_volatile, atomics, or a compiler fence before request_pendsv_pending(). Your SCB path uses DSB/ISB, which helps the device see the write; it does not by itself stop the compiler from reordering earlier stores to globals. Worth tightening at the API boundary.